    <string name="setup_s1_title">1. Allow Camera &amp; Location</string>
    <string name="setup_s1_body">reWatt uses the camera to detect who is in the room, and location to fetch outdoor weather for energy advice.</string>
    <string name="setup_perm_camera">Camera</string>
    <string name="setup_perm_location">Location</string>
    <string name="setup_allowed">Allowed</string>
    <string name="setup_not_allowed">Not allowed</string>
    <string name="setup_allow_permissions">Allow Permissions</string>
    <string name="setup_s2_title">2. Turn Off Battery Saver for reWatt</string>
    <string name="setup_s2_body">Your phone may pause the app to save battery. Turn off Battery Optimization so reWatt keeps running at all times — even when the screen is off.</string>
    <string name="setup_batt_off">Battery Saver is off — good!</string>
    <string name="setup_batt_on">Battery Saver is on — set it to Off!</string>
    <string name="setup_allow_always_on">Open Battery Saver settings</string>
    <string name="setup_s3_title">4. Mount the Sensor Phone</string>
    <string name="setup_s3_body">Use the wall mount in the kit to attach this phone to a wall or metal surface. Point the camera toward the centre of the room.</string>
    <string name="setup_mount_photo">Mount photo — coming soon</string>
    <string name="setup_s3_tip1">Attach the mount at shoulder height or above.</string>
    <string name="setup_s3_tip2">Make sure the camera faces the seating area.</string>
    <string name="setup_s3_tip3">Keep the lens clear — no tape or cover over it.</string>
    <string name="setup_s3_tip4">Plug in the charger so the phone stays powered.</string>
    <string name="setup_s4_title">5. Check the Sensor View</string>
    <string name="setup_s4_body">Ask the person with the Admin phone to open the Capture tab and choose your hall. They will confirm the camera can see the whole room clearly.</string>
    <string name="setup_example_view">Example view — coming soon</string>
    <string name="setup_s4_tip1">The full room should be visible — no blind spots.</string>
    <string name="setup_s4_tip2">Avoid pointing at bright light sources.</string>
    <string name="setup_s4_tip3">If the angle is wrong, re-adjust the mount and check again.</string>
    <string name="setup_s5_title">6. Name Your Space</string>
    <string name="setup_s5_body">Give this sensor a name — e.g. the room, community hall or residence area it monitors.</string>
    <string name="setup_space_name">Space name</string>
    <string name="setup_space_name_hint">e.g. Room1, Living room, Community hall</string>
    <string name="setup_s6_title">7. You\'re All Set!</string>
    <string name="setup_s6_body">Everything is ready. reWatt will now watch the room and help manage energy automatically. You can come back to this guide anytime from the Settings tab.</string>
    <string name="setup_complete">Setup complete</string>
    <string name="setup_complete_desc">Tap Done to start using reWatt.</string>
